>> title: Florentines
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: almonds, chocolate, candied orange, italian, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: florentine cookies, Florentiner, lace cookies
>> servings: 24
>> time: 1 hour
>> step.2: boil in a saucepan to 238°F (114°C)
>> step.4: bake in spoonfuls 350°F (175°C) 10 min

Heat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C) and line two #baking sheets{} with parchment.

Bring @heavy cream{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(57 g), @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g), and @honey{2%Tbs}(42 g) to a boil in a #saucepan{} and cook to 238°F.

Stir @sliced almonds{1 1/2%cup}(130 g), @candied orange peel{1/3%cup}(60 g), @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(16 g), and @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g) into @&(~1)syrup{}.

Bake @&(~1)batter{} in spoonfuls at 350°F for ~{10%min}.

Melt @dark chocolate{6%oz}(170 g; chopped).

Spread @&(~1)melted chocolate{} on the flat side of @&(~2)cooled florentines{}.
